Thanks for the triage. I investigated the issue further and prepared a local fix based on the dense `_incremental_mean_and_var` update.

The updated implementation handles the zero-observation cases explicitly:

- preserves existing statistics when a new batch has zero valid observations for a feature;
- allows features with no previous observations to establish their statistics when valid values arrive later;
- handles zero-weight batches without contributing to the variance;
- avoids unnecessary pooling/squared-value calculations for zero-count features;
- explicitly handles the case where the total observation count is zero.

I also added regression coverage for the reported case, weighted/unweighted inputs, zero-weight batches, large-mean overflow cases, first valid observations arriving later, and Array API zero-count combinations.

The targeted checks pass, although I have not been able to run the native pytest suite because my local checkout is missing the compiled scikit-learn build.

The changes are currently on my local branch `fix/dense-incremental-all-nan-variance`, but I have not opened a PR yet.

Would this approach be appropriate for #35070? If the issue is considered actionable, I'm happy to open the PR for review.

Thanks for the issue, it does seem like an oversight indeed since the documentation says
